  "notes": "ES modules. An import of a name re-exported by a barrel resolves to the *origin* file (the barrel is a hop, recorded on the importing file as one edge with `barrel_hop`); a barrel's own export set is empty because it declares nothing. A default export is the exported name `default`, and the local name is an alias. Two `export interface Config` blocks in one file are declaration merging: one symbol, two declaration sites. A module-level binding whose initialiser is a function value is a `fn`, not a `var`. Members are excluded from the export set.",
